THE ONE CONDITION. The credit line, and its link to https://rrw-ads.com, must
stay visible in the rendered page. Not in a comment, not in a colophon on another
page, not hidden with CSS, and not marked rel="nofollow": visible to the person
using the calculator, on the page where the calculator runs, as a working and
followable link.

Restyle the credit to match your site. Move it. Change its wording so it reads
naturally in your voice. It just has to be there, and the link has to work.

WHY IT DIFFERS FROM THE MIT CODE ABOVE. Everything else here is MIT precisely
because we want it used with no strings. This one directory is the exception: the
link is the only thing we get for building it, and it is the whole price. If
that trade does not suit you, the MIT-licensed parser under
tools/search-term-report/ asks for nothing at all.

NO WARRANTY. The arithmetic is exact for the values entered. Whether those values
